From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: let the memory arena name a platform

This SDK's libc++ ends its config-site block with `#undef __FreeBSD__`, which is deliberate: it
is how a libc++ built against musl is steered to its musl support path rather than FreeBSD's
(see <__locale>, which would otherwise want FreeBSD's <xlocale.h>, and <locale>, whose
_LIBCPP_GET_C_LOCALE would stop matching the prebuilt libc++.a). The cost is that a C++ TU on
this platform sees NO platform macro at all - not _WIN32, not __linux__, not __APPLE__, not
__FreeBSD__ - while every C TU in the same binary sees __FreeBSD__ == 12.

memory_arena is where that surfaces as an error rather than as a wrong branch:

    memory_arena.cpp:101: use of undeclared identifier 'm_shmem_fd'
    memory_arena.cpp:112: #error Unknown platform.
    memory_arena.cpp:115: use of undeclared identifier 'pid'

__ORBIS__ is always defined here, so it is the macro to name.

The arena itself STAYS UNIMPLEMENTED, and that is the intended outcome rather than a shortcut.
Its POSIX arm needs shm_open, which this SDK has in neither its headers nor libc.a, so it would
be an undefined symbol at link. Create() therefore falls through to the existing `return false`,
which is a case the caller already handles - the arena backs fastmem, and swanstation runs
without it. What the two hunks buy is that the file COMPILES and IsValid() has a field to read.

diff --git a/src/common/memory_arena.cpp b/src/common/memory_arena.cpp
index e152428..23c7f4f 100644
--- a/src/common/memory_arena.cpp
+++ b/src/common/memory_arena.cpp
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ Log_SetChannel(Common::MemoryArena);
 #include <sys/ioctl.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
-#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__ORBIS__)
 #include <cerrno>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ static std::string GetFileMappingName()
 {
 #if defined(_WIN32)
   const unsigned pid = GetCurrentProcessId();
-#elif defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__linux__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__linux__) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__ORBIS__)
   const unsigned pid = static_cast<unsigned>(getpid());
 #else
 #error Unknown platform.
diff --git a/src/common/memory_arena.h b/src/common/memory_arena.h
index 655b6a0..5ceedbf 100644
--- a/src/common/memory_arena.h
+++ b/src/common/memory_arena.h
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ public:
 private:
 #if defined(_WIN32)
   void* m_file_handle = nullptr;
-#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(ANDROID) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(ANDROID) || defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__ORBIS__)
   int m_shmem_fd = -1;
 #endif
 
